# Context

T066 hardening follow-ups after the boundary landed. The byte
model changed shape: maxMessageBytes now bounds one message
(request, or one registration) instead of request+registrations
combined, so a warm bundle no longer re-pays its bytes on every
submit. Registration refusal surfaces at assign time because that
is the first moment the parent knows which worker lacks the bundle.

Unicode-first compileRaw mirrors validator.ts compilePattern on
purpose: pattern synthesis (gateway/pattern.ts) probes candidates
with regex-test while the validator accepts instances with the same
pattern; divergent flags would let a schema-valid value refuse its
own synthesized probe.

The hostile-pattern probe is a heuristic lint, not a proof: it
derives its battery from the pattern's own literal characters,
where nearly every catastrophic shape trips. Benign patterns answer
in microseconds, so a 100 ms miss is hostile with near certainty.
False negatives are acceptable; the serving boundary bounds the
cost regardless.
